1
00:00:03,929 --> 00:00:09,427
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Makkan period by Imam Anwar Al-Awlaki.

2
00:00:09,555 --> 00:00:13,873
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:15,145 --> 00:00:19,034
Yesterday we talked about the importance of studying Seerah(سيرة).

4
00:00:19,747 --> 00:00:28,327
And now we'll start with the first session on Seerah(سيرة), itself.

5
00:00:28,835 --> 00:00:36,692
Now usually the authors or the scholars, who write about the life of Muhammadﷺ,

6
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:40,828
they do not usually start talking about his birth.

7
00:00:41,756 --> 00:00:44,772
They would go a little bit before that,

8
00:00:45,574 --> 00:00:49,582
actually about few thousand years before that

9
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:56,168
and they would talk about his father Ibrahim عليه السلام.

10
00:00:56,494 --> 00:01:00,964
That's usually where they would start talking about Rasool Allah ﷺ,

11
00:01:01,004 --> 00:01:06,153
they would talk about his ancestry, starting by Ibrahim عليه السلام.

12
00:01:06,269 --> 00:01:12,198
The emphasis is on the Hajar(هاجر) and Ismail(اسماعيل) side of the story rather than the, Is'haaq(اسحاق) and Sarah(ساره),

13
00:01:13,091 --> 00:01:15,813
because that's the lineage of Muhammadﷺ.

14
00:01:17,297 --> 00:01:22,194
So, they would start by talking about the story of Ibrahim علبه السلام, Hajar(هاجر) and Sarah(ساره),

15
00:01:22,477 --> 00:01:25,415
when they traveled to Hijaz(حجاز).

16
00:01:26,599 --> 00:01:33,596
Ibrahim عليه السلام, his wife and his newborn son, traveled into Arabia, into the land of Hijaz(حجاز).

17
00:01:35,003 --> 00:01:39,281
And Ibrahim(ابراهيم) took them to present day Makkah.

18
00:01:40,384 --> 00:01:42,075
At that time, there was nothing there,

19
00:01:42,956 --> 00:01:45,789
nobody was living there, there was no cultivation.

20
00:01:46,170 --> 00:01:47,972
It was a dead Valley.

21
00:01:49,535 --> 00:01:52,859
But the place where the House of Allah is built,

22
00:01:52,939 --> 00:01:56,689
the place where the Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه) was built was sacred, since the world was created.

23
00:01:57,614 --> 00:02:01,479
In fact, there's a difference of opinion on who is the first one to build Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه).

24
00:02:02,495 --> 00:02:06,002
The majority opinion is that it was Ibrahim عليه السلام

25
00:02:06,073 --> 00:02:09,137
but there are some scholars, who say that Adam(آدم) was the first one to build it.

26
00:02:10,146 --> 00:02:15,130
Now, regardless of whether Ibrahimعليه السلام or Adamعليه السلام built it,

27
00:02:15,345 --> 00:02:21,511
the place itself, whether there was a building on it or not, was holy and sacred from day one.

28
00:02:23,067 --> 00:02:33,610
Ibrahim عليه السلام and his wife and son, arrived to the valley and in the place where Zam-Zam(زمزم) is currently,

29
00:02:34,376 --> 00:02:36,384
obviously there wasn't Zam-Zam(زمزم) at that time.

30
00:02:37,464 --> 00:02:42,711
Ibrahim عليه السلام left his wife and son, Ismael(اسماعيل).

31
00:02:44,003 --> 00:02:47,969
He left with them some water and a leather bag of dates.

32
00:02:49,297 --> 00:02:50,355
And he walked away.

33
00:02:50,911 --> 00:02:53,757
He just turned away and left.

34
00:02:54,845 --> 00:02:58,917
Now, Hajarعليها السّلام knew that Ya'ani(يعني) Ibrahimعليه السلام was gonna leave them

35
00:02:58,957 --> 00:03:03,297
but she didn't expect to be left in such a place, in the middle of the desert.

36
00:03:04,908 --> 00:03:07,638
So, she followed him and she said:

37
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:14,845
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم)! Are you gonna leave us in a place where there's no cultivation and there's no one living.?

38
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:18,352
Ibrahim عليه السلام did not answer back.

39
00:03:19,614 --> 00:03:22,019
She asked him again, no response,

40
00:03:22,741 --> 00:03:25,583
she asked him a third time, he didn't answer back,

41
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:28,511
and then Hajarعليها السّلام said:

42
00:03:28,829 --> 00:03:31,104
آلَّهُ اَمَرَكَ بِهَذَا

43
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:33,863
Did Allah tell you to do so?.

44
00:03:35,432 --> 00:03:37,416
Ibrahimعليه السلام said: Yes.

45
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:39,838
قَالَتْ فَلَنْ يُضَيِّعَنَ اِذَنْ

46
00:03:40,208 --> 00:03:42,155
Then Allah will take care of us.

47
00:03:43,424 --> 00:03:48,083
If this is a command from Allah, then I have trust in Allah that He will take care of us.

48
00:03:48,392 --> 00:03:51,373
Look at the faith of this woman,

49
00:03:52,093 --> 00:03:53,406
in the middle of nowhere.

50
00:03:53,852 --> 00:03:57,901
But if this is the command of Allah, I have trusted in Allah, Allah will take care of us.

51
00:03:58,025 --> 00:03:59,319
فَلَنْ يُضَيِّعَنَ الله

52
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:02,316
Allah will not waste us, Allah will not neglect us.

53
00:04:04,273 --> 00:04:08,972
Ibrahim عليه السلام left and when he reached to a place where they cannot see him anymore.

54
00:04:09,876 --> 00:04:15,792
Ibrahimعليه السلام turned around and faced Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) or the place of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

55
00:04:17,456 --> 00:04:18,988
And he made Dua(دُعَا) to Allah.

56
00:04:19,397 --> 00:04:20,108
He said:

57
00:04:20,432 --> 00:04:34,223
رَبَّنَا إِنِّي أَسْكَنْتُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِي بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِي زَرْعٍ عِنْدَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِ

58
00:04:34,525 --> 00:04:43,747
رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ فَاجْعَلْ أَفْئِدَةً مِنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِي إِلَيْهِمْ

59
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:51,990
وَارْزُقْهُمْ مِنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُونَ۝

60
00:04:53,416 --> 00:05:05,750
Ibrahimعليه السلام said: O Allah, I'm leaving my offspring, in infertile land, a land where there is, no cultivation.

61
00:05:05,787 --> 00:05:07,384
بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِي زَرْعٍ

62
00:05:08,345 --> 00:05:10,511
Next to your sacred house.

63
00:05:10,956 --> 00:05:14,479
So, the place was known that it was sacred even though Al-Ka'aba(الكعبه) wasn't built.

64
00:05:15,736 --> 00:05:18,019
And then Ibrahimعليه السلام made a Dua(دُعَا).

65
00:05:18,974 --> 00:05:24,543
Now, you know the Maslow hierarchy of needs, the pyramid?

66
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:26,924
What is the foundation of the pyramid?

67
00:05:27,063 --> 00:05:27,761
The bottom!

68
00:05:28,031 --> 00:05:31,586
What is the first human need that needs to be satisfied?

69
00:05:31,991 --> 00:05:32,964
What does it start with?

70
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:35,098
First thing is what?

71
00:05:35,622 --> 00:05:37,027
Physiological needs, right?

72
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:38,654
That's the bottom of the pyramid.

73
00:05:39,351 --> 00:05:42,948
So, that is the most important need for humans.

74
00:05:43,332 --> 00:05:44,412
That's the base of the pyramid.

75
00:05:44,475 --> 00:05:47,382
And then what's after that, what's the next step,

76
00:05:48,115 --> 00:05:49,082
Psychological,

77
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,145
and then the third,

78
00:05:52,026 --> 00:05:52,841
Social,

79
00:05:53,941 --> 00:05:55,807
Physiological on the bottom,

80
00:05:55,923 --> 00:05:56,927
Social,

81
00:05:57,561 --> 00:05:58,567
Spiritual,

82
00:05:58,887 --> 00:06:01,730
and then the peak is, Self-actualization.

83
00:06:02,596 --> 00:06:03,434
So, that's the pyramid.

84
00:06:03,632 --> 00:06:11,050
First of all, as a human being you want to satisfy the physiological necessary needs which are food and shelter.

85
00:06:12,486 --> 00:06:19,516
After that, you want to have friends, have a social life, have a belonging, an Association.

86
00:06:20,784 --> 00:06:22,829
So, those are the social needs,

87
00:06:23,315 --> 00:06:26,868
and then you have the spiritual needs.

88
00:06:27,371 --> 00:06:31,553
So, after you have achieved the physiological needs and the social needs

89
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:35,618
after that, you start thinking about religion, according to Maslow.

90
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:40,609
Finally, you have the self-actualization, which is on the top of the pyramid.

91
00:06:42,188 --> 00:06:46,141
But according to Ibrahimعليه السّلام, the pyramid is inverted.

92
00:06:47,728 --> 00:06:52,060
The first thing that he asked for was not food and drink or shelter.

93
00:06:52,863 --> 00:06:54,502
The first thing he asked for, was:

94
00:06:54,582 --> 00:06:55,963
 رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ

95
00:06:56,823 --> 00:07:00,323
The first thing that they asked for even though it would make sense that they would ask for...

96
00:07:00,506 --> 00:07:07,501
I mean, we would assume that Ibrahimعليه السّلام, since he left them in a valley where there's, there's no cultivation,

97
00:07:07,569 --> 00:07:12,311
the first thing he would ask for is to provide his family with food, for their survival.

98
00:07:12,776 --> 00:07:15,753
But Ibrahimعليه السلام started in his Dua(دُعَا) by saying;

99
00:07:15,793 --> 00:07:17,059
 رَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ

100
00:07:17,577 --> 00:07:20,540
O Allah so that, they may establish prayer.

101
00:07:21,696 --> 00:07:23,677
So, the first need that he asked for,

102
00:07:23,879 --> 00:07:28,462
or the first thing that he mentioned, was spiritual needs, Salah(صلاة),

103
00:07:28,855 --> 00:07:29,871
اِقَامَةِ الصَّلَاةْ

104
00:07:29,990 --> 00:07:31,362
Establishing the prayers

105
00:07:32,188 --> 00:07:33,425
and then he said:

106
00:07:33,768 --> 00:07:36,399
 فَاجْعَلْ أَفْئِدَةً مِنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِي إِلَيْهِمْ

107
00:07:36,711 --> 00:07:42,720
And then make or put their love, in hearts of people.

108
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,296
 Ya'ani(يعني) make people love them.

109
00:07:44,704 --> 00:07:49,635
So, he is asking Allahسبحانه وتعالى to draw people to his family,

110
00:07:50,157 --> 00:07:52,038
and to make them love his family.

111
00:07:52,569 --> 00:07:54,480
So, he's asking for the social needs,

112
00:07:54,934 --> 00:07:57,188
and then finally he said:

113
00:07:57,383 --> 00:07:58,915
وَارْزُقْهُمْ مِنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ

114
00:07:59,248 --> 00:08:01,721
Then provide them with fruits.

115
00:08:03,029 --> 00:08:08,664
So, Ibrahimعليه السلام is starting by asking for Salah(صلاة), spiritual needs

116
00:08:08,704 --> 00:08:12,923
and then social needs and then physiological needs.

117
00:08:13,649 --> 00:08:18,732
But even when he asked Allahسبحانه وتعالى to provide them with Samaraat(ثمرات), fruits,

118
00:08:19,101 --> 00:08:22,093
he also connected it, to Ibadah(عبادة) and said:

119
00:08:22,118 --> 00:08:23,390
لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُونَ

120
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:24,945
So, that they may be grateful.

121
00:08:25,299 --> 00:08:29,489
So, even when he was asking Allah to provide them with worldly things,

122
00:08:29,696 --> 00:08:32,099
he was still connecting it to religion.

123
00:08:32,903 --> 00:08:34,053
لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُونَ

124
00:08:34,235 --> 00:08:37,180
Give them fruit, so that they will be grateful to you.

125
00:08:38,998 --> 00:08:44,609
And that is true self-actualization, when Allah becomes everything for you.

126
00:08:46,387 --> 00:08:50,196
When you're eating, when you're drinking, when you're sleeping, you're doing everything for Allah.

127
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:58,418
That is the true tranquility and that is the self-actualization that neither did Maslow, or anybody else achieve,

128
00:08:58,815 --> 00:09:01,571
except the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah and Aouliyaa(أولياء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

129
00:09:03,887 --> 00:09:05,712
And then Ibrahimعليه السّلام left.

130
00:09:07,712 --> 00:09:12,942
Hajar(هَاجر) made use of the small amount of food that he left with them,

131
00:09:13,704 --> 00:09:18,236
but obviously after a short while they ran out of food

132
00:09:19,522 --> 00:09:23,498
and Hajarعليها السّلام was breastfeeding Ismail(اسماعيل)

133
00:09:24,284 --> 00:09:29,172
and her milk was drying up, because she's thirsty and hungry.

134
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:35,011
And now Ismailعليه السّلام is beginning to cry, he's hungry.

135
00:09:36,442 --> 00:09:43,458
So, Hajarعليها السّلام couldn't afford seeing her son, agonizing in pain.

136
00:09:44,736 --> 00:09:48,657
So, she left him and she started climbing a hill.

137
00:09:49,331 --> 00:09:53,431
A Hill, which was called later As-Saffa(ألصفاء).

138
00:09:54,276 --> 00:09:58,276
She climbed on top of that hill to see, if she can see anybody in the horizon.

139
00:09:59,331 --> 00:10:03,284
She would look left and right, and would see no one.

140
00:10:04,014 --> 00:10:05,768
So, she would climb down the hill.

141
00:10:06,125 --> 00:10:10,831
And when she would reach the valley, she would tuck up her clothes and run.

142
00:10:11,379 --> 00:10:13,680
And then she would climb another Hill,

143
00:10:14,069 --> 00:10:16,704
which was later called Al-Marwa(ألمروة).

144
00:10:17,482 --> 00:10:22,704
And she would reach the top and look in the horizon, if she can see anybody.

145
00:10:24,665 --> 00:10:30,022
And her son is twisting and turning in pain.

146
00:10:31,641 --> 00:10:36,974
And Hajarعليها السّلام is running up and down, these hills and she did that seven times.

147
00:10:38,290 --> 00:10:42,966
The seventh time, when she reached the top of the hill.

148
00:10:43,482 --> 00:10:44,847
She heard a sound

149
00:10:47,068 --> 00:10:50,593
and she was staring around to see where that sound is coming from.

150
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:59,535
And to her amazement, she saw that the sound was coming from beneath the feet of Ismailعليه السّلام.

151
00:11:00,996 --> 00:11:06,260
Jibreelعليه السلام descended and was digging the well of Zam-Zam(زمزم).

152
00:11:06,866 --> 00:11:10,807
And the water was coming out from beneath his feet.

153
00:11:11,276 --> 00:11:16,347
Hajarعليها السلام was rushing in happiness to the source of the water.

154
00:11:16,661 --> 00:11:21,063
And because it's a dry desert, and it would soak up, all of the water.

155
00:11:21,169 --> 00:11:24,872
She was making a pool around the water to contain it.

156
00:11:25,547 --> 00:11:29,031
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was narrating the story, he said:

157
00:11:29,078 --> 00:11:35,084
رَحِمَ اللهُ اُمُّ اِسْمَاعِيْلْ لَوْ تَرَكَتْهَا لَكَانَتْ زَمْزَمْ عَيْنَنْ تَجْرِيْ

158
00:11:35,436 --> 00:11:36,578
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

159
00:11:36,635 --> 00:11:39,702
May Allah have mercy, on the mother of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل),

160
00:11:39,967 --> 00:11:44,402
if she would have left the water alone, it would have been a flowing river.

161
00:11:45,208 --> 00:11:49,053
But because of her interference it was a well,

162
00:11:49,321 --> 00:11:54,591
 she was trying to contain the water and she didn't allow it to flow.

163
00:11:55,186 --> 00:12:01,986
If she would have left the miracle as it was going without interfering, it would have been a flowing stream.

164
00:12:02,419 --> 00:12:05,387
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and said: May Allah have mercy on her.

165
00:12:07,982 --> 00:12:11,307
Hajarعليها السّلام, Think for a moment.

166
00:12:12,895 --> 00:12:19,538
What were her feelings, when she was running up and down those hills?

167
00:12:20,824 --> 00:12:24,863
Her heart must have been broken, she might have been crying

168
00:12:26,578 --> 00:12:32,228
because of the pain and suffering of seeing her son die in front of her eyes.

169
00:12:33,054 --> 00:12:38,625
Hajar(هَاجر) was a believing woman, she was a righteous woman,

170
00:12:39,538 --> 00:12:41,490
and Allahسبحانه وتعالى was testing her,

171
00:12:42,625 --> 00:12:48,030
and Allahسبحانه وتعالى was hiding for her something in the future that she didn't know.

172
00:12:49,522 --> 00:13:00,312
So, at that time, naturally as a mother, she must have been in an extreme pain, seeing her son crying,

173
00:13:01,366 --> 00:13:05,816
 and she's in the middle of nowhere, running up and down these mountains.

174
00:13:07,617 --> 00:13:13,887
Now, just imagine if Hajar(هَاجر) was resurrected at the time of Hajj(حج)

175
00:13:14,689 --> 00:13:20,294
and she would have a chance to see, what Muslims from all over the world are doing.?

176
00:13:20,808 --> 00:13:22,718
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

177
00:13:22,799 --> 00:13:27,354
When he was mentioning the story of Hajar(هَاجر) going up and down As-Saffa Wal Marwa(ألصفا والمروة),

178
00:13:27,689 --> 00:13:28,921
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

179
00:13:29,155 --> 00:13:32,855
And that is why.? We go between Al-Saffah(الصَّفا) and Marwa(مَروَاة).

180
00:13:33,443 --> 00:13:37,356
So, we are following the footsteps of Hajarعليها السّلام.

181
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:45,792
We are going up and down As-Saffa Wal Marwa(ألصفا والمروة) to follow the footsteps of our mother Hajarعليها السّلام.

182
00:13:46,704 --> 00:13:54,384
if Hajar(هَاجر) knew that the time will come, when people will come from the four corners of the world,

183
00:13:54,887 --> 00:14:00,027
to follow her footsteps in millions, to do what she did.

184
00:14:01,490 --> 00:14:05,475
She would have went through As-Saffa Wal Marwa(ألصفا والمروة) with, the big smile on her face.

185
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:13,114
So, dear brothers and sisters, as a Muslim, as a believer when you are going through these trials,

186
00:14:13,187 --> 00:14:16,572
you might have a certain mindset, you might have a certain feeling,

187
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,713
but you don't know what's waiting for you on the other side.

188
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:22,895
You don't know what Allah is hiding for you in the future.

189
00:14:23,641 --> 00:14:25,649
This is the gift, this is the present,

190
00:14:26,165 --> 00:14:29,157
that Allahسبحانه وتعالى has given Hajar(هَاجر) in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

191
00:14:30,022 --> 00:14:32,649
Just think about what Allahسبحانه وتعالى will give her in Aakhirah(آخِرَة).

192
00:14:33,919 --> 00:14:40,085
